u}$ decays were detected, resulting in a branching ratio upper limit of $0.85$ at $90\%$ confidence level. This finding is consistent with the predictions of the Standard Model and significantly improves upon previous searches by nearly a factor of three, while still falling short of achieving the sensitivity required to precisely measure the decay rate through $K^+ightarrow\pi^+
u ar{
u}$ in the future.
